      "text": "ANALYSIS FRAMEWORK:"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ANTITRUST.md#010",
      "path": [
        "04-ANTITRUST.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:law:04-antitrust, git-history:law:04-antitrust]",
        "canonical_path": "law/04-ANTITRUST.md",
        "concepts": "[antitrust]",
        "current_path": "law/04-ANTITRUST.md",
        "id": "maxim:law:antitrust",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "law",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[antitrust]",
        "section": "law",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "04 - Antitrust Law",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PER SE ILLEGAL: certain conduct presumed anticompetitive without market analysis\n    Price fixing: horizontal agreements on price (including price floors/ceilings)\n    Bid rigging: coordination on competitive bids\n    Market division: horizontal competitors divide markets/customers\n    Group boycotts (naked): horizontal competitors agree to refuse to deal\n    → Conduct is condemned categorically; no efficiencies defense available"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ANTITRUST.md#011",
      "path": [
        "04-ANTITRUST.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:law:04-antitrust, git-history:law:04-antitrust]",
        "canonical_path": "law/04-ANTITRUST.md",
        "concepts": "[antitrust]",
        "current_path": "law/04-ANTITRUST.md",
        "id": "maxim:law:antitrust",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "law",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[antitrust]",
        "section": "law",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "04 - Antitrust Law",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "RULE OF REASON: weighing procompetitive vs anticompetitive effects\n    Plaintiff must prove: anticompetitive harm in a relevant market\n    Burden shifts to defendant: procompetitive justifications\n    Burden shifts back to plaintiff: less restrictive alternative exists\n    Most vertical restraints analyzed under rule of reason\n    Some horizontal conduct (IP licensing, joint ventures) analyzed under RoR"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ANTITRUST.md#012",
      "path": [
        "04-ANTITRUST.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:law:04-antitrust, git-history:law:04-antitrust]",
        "canonical_path": "law/04-ANTITRUST.md",
        "concepts": "[antitrust]",
        "current_path": "law/04-ANTITRUST.md",
        "id": "maxim:law:antitrust",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "law",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[antitrust]",
        "section": "law",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "04 - Antitrust Law",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "QUICK LOOK: abbreviated rule of reason for obviously anticompetitive conduct\n    Without elaborate inquiry, anticompetitive effect presumed\n    Defendant must provide plausible efficiency justification or lose\n```"
    },
